# LeakSanitizer exceptions for the sanitizer builds (tests/CMakeLists.txt). Each entry is
# memory SatDump keeps on purpose for its whole run; the system frees it at exit. Anything
# else that leaks fails the tests (exit code 86).
#
# The planet-position file (resources/spice/de440s.bsp) opened once at start-up
# (src-core/init.cpp) and used by SuperNOVAS until exit. Closing it at exit could leave a
# thread that is still running with a freed handle, which is worse than this one allocation.
leak:calceph_spice_cache_init
